From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: meson: pll_v4: do not clamp frac to frac_max, pick a valid table entry

Fixes found by the S905X5/CoreELEC driver review:

- F055 drivers/clk/meson/clk-pll.c:1357: pll_v4 frac is clamped to frac_max (a whole m step), so any rate outside [m, m+1) jumps to the wrong table entry or pins at m+1 (the S7D HIFI tuning range)

See the review diary (S905X5-DRIVER-REVIEW-DIARY.md) for the defect
analysis and the forum discussion.

final judge sign-off did not run, so this patch still needs a human
read before it is proposed upstream. Not yet exercised on S905X5 hardware.

diff --git a/drivers/clk/meson/clk-pll.c b/drivers/clk/meson/clk-pll.c
index 92df24b..b98d5a4 100644

--- a/drivers/clk/meson/clk-pll.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/meson/clk-pll.c
@@ -1613,7 +1613,8 @@ static int meson_clk_pll_v4_set_rate(struct clk_hw *hw, unsigned long rate,
 		    frac != meson_parm_read(clk->map, &pll->frac))
 			/* Clear frac bits and Update frac value */
 			meson_parm_write(clk->map, &pll->frac, frac);
-		if (od != meson_parm_read(clk->map, &pll->od))
+		if (MESON_PARM_APPLICABLE(&pll->od) &&
+		    od != meson_parm_read(clk->map, &pll->od))
 			/* Clear od bits and Update od value */
 			meson_parm_write(clk->map, &pll->od, od);
 
